{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1351268-questions-about-damage-types-in-combat-with-spirits-in-both-versions-of-cod","id":1351268,"title":"Questions about damage types in combat with spirits in both versions of CoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-27T06:17:17-08:00","id":1351268,"title":"Questions about damage types in combat with spirits in both versions of CoD","content":"<span style=\"color:#1D1D1D\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">I was checking the nWoD 2nd edition spirit rules and I noticed spirits now take bashing damage when manifested. That wasn't the case in the 1st edition, was it? I believe they were immune for physical combat back then. Did they change that? Or was that only ghosts? And how about the combat in the spirit world itself? Did that change as well? I know the best thing for fighting spirits is either holy damage or an exorcism, but I see they use banes as well now.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#1D1D1D\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So basically I want to know if you would fight a manifested spirit with a knive or a gun in the real world what kind of damage would you do? And if you would fight a spirit with a knive or a gun in the spirit world or Hisil what kind of damage would you do? I am curious about both the 1st and the 2nd edition of the nWoD or CoD. I have the Book of Spirits on pdf and I just can't find it in those big blocks of text WoD books usually have. I find a lot of other things, but I can't seem to find what I am looking for.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T07:08:01-08:00","id":1351279,"title":"","content":"Mundane weapons always do bashing damage to ephemeral, because they lack blood and internal organs.<br /> Special powers and the entity bane can inflict more severe damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T16:04:17-08:00","id":1351376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1351268-questions-about-damage-types-in-combat-with-spirits-in-both-versions-of-cod?p=1351279#post1351279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mundane weapons always do bashing damage to ephemeral, because they lack blood and internal organs.<br /> Special powers and the entity bane can inflict more severe damage</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, gr8. Was that always the case in the original 2004 core rules? Or did they change that in the revised rulebook? I know that ghosts were pretty much invincible to mundane weapons in the core rulebook. So they changed that to bashing damage. But spirits I can't find anything about that in the original rules. I could of course update to the new ruleset, but last time I checked I wasn't that happy with all the fiddly beats, tilts and conditions in that ruleset.<br /> <br /> The thing is I want to build a new setting that focuses mostly on mortal hunters/investigators (possibly with psychic powers) investigating mortals who dabble with forces that should really be left alone. I want to include cultists, hedge witches/ritual magicians and the spirit world. So I checked around and no other horror/urban fantasy does anything similar with dark animism like the World of Darkness does. Most of them have either dead people/ghosts or some sort of demons or it Cthulhu. So I guess I just might use the WoD again, but it's been a while since I used that system. <br /> <br /> I checked the new core rules and despite the fact I am not that fond on the fiddly bits, I did find some pretty cool stuff in there that mechanically supports what I have in mind. There are psychic merits, rules for spirits and numina, rules for horrors and dread powers and a lot of equipment. The equipment and psychic powers support my pc's and with the rules for creating ephemeral beings and horrors I can make all the monsters I want. Great. That covers most of what I need.<br /> <br /> Now all I need are some sanity mechanics and some rules for ritual magic like stuff you can find in BRP's Enlightened magic, Nephilim's Liber Ka or Conspiracy X's Paranormal Sourcebook. Low powered magic that is complicated to cast and takes a while to do so. Not the spellslinging Vancian magic you find in a lot fantasy rpg's. Last time I checked I believe Second Sight did something like that. Are there some new ritual magic rules in a new book that I missed? Or do I need to make a conversion of those rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T16:12:04-08:00","id":1351377,"title":"","content":"Note: physical weapons cannot normally interact with ephemeral entities, meaning they normally cause no damage; it's just that if a physical weapon is somehow given the ability to interact with an ephemeral entity (or the ephemeral entity physically manifests) it will still only do bashing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T21:23:42-08:00","id":1351409,"title":"","content":"Remember also - 'Killing' manifesting ephemeral IS NOT literal destruction of being. It's just ending Manifestetion. So shooting to ghost or spirit in CoD can end their Manifestation - but those beings can return to existance in simply few hours later, with next Manifestation cast. \ud83d\ude0e &lt; Taking from Supernatural &gt; You still need to burn bones to truly kill ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T03:11:02-08:00","id":1351439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1351268-questions-about-damage-types-in-combat-with-spirits-in-both-versions-of-cod?p=1351409#post1351409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember also - 'Killing' manifesting ephemeral IS NOT literal destruction of being. It's just ending Manifestetion. So shooting to ghost or spirit in CoD can end their Manifestation - but those beings can return to existance in simply few hours later, with next Manifestation cast. \ud83d\ude0e &lt; Taking from Supernatural &gt; You still need to burn bones to truly kill ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only Banes forcefully end Manifestations (and only some of them). <i>Shooting</i> a spirit (unless bullets is its Bane) will damage it without forcing it to stop Manifesting. If it takes the spirit to full lethal it'll discorporate, just as if you shot it to full lethal inside the Shadow. Once discorporated it takes a lot more than a few hours to return.<br /> <br /> Also, burning the bones of a ghost doesn't do anything <i>unless</i> the bones happened to be the only remaining Anchor, in which case it takes a couple of hours for the ghost to get sucked down into the Underworld, depending on how much Essence it has left. At least it won't be able to use any Manifestations after losing its last Anchor unless it's Rank 4+ or something else provides Manifestation Conditions for it (such as a Bound's Liminal Aura or Plasm from GtSE). It'll still be fully able to use its Influences until it gets sucked down, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T15:34:57-08:00","id":1351726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1351268-questions-about-damage-types-in-combat-with-spirits-in-both-versions-of-cod?p=1351377#post1351377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: physical weapons cannot normally interact with ephemeral entities, meaning they normally cause no damage; it's just that if a physical weapon is somehow given the ability to interact with an ephemeral entity (or the ephemeral entity physically manifests) it will still only do bashing damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that is completely true. I just read the core rules and I believe it says you do bashing damage with mundane weapons to ghosts and spirits. In the old ruleset from 2004 you couldn't hit ghosts with mundane weapons so they changed that with this ruleset. I don't know if that was the case with spirits. I do have a pdf copy of the Book of Spirits, but I can't find it in there. Maybe I am overlooking it.<br /> <br /> I see in the new ruleset they have made some sort of sanity system called Integrity, so that's great. I was looking for that as well. So I only need to make a conversion of the Second Sight magic system or just use the old rules instead. But I do like the complete package the new ruleset offers. I think the core rules provide for the same stuff you needed at least four books in the previous edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1873,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","user":"Jan Paparazzi","date":". 11-29-2019, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1873-jan-paparazzi","name":"Jan Paparazzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1873_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"257"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T18:52:42-08:00","id":1351760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jan Paparazzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1351268-questions-about-damage-types-in-combat-with-spirits-in-both-versions-of-cod?p=1351726#post1351726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that is completely true. I just read the core rules and I believe it says you do bashing damage with mundane weapons to ghosts and spirits. In the old ruleset from 2004 you couldn't hit ghosts with mundane weapons so they changed that with this ruleset. I don't know if that was the case with spirits. I do have a pdf copy of the Book of Spirits, but I can't find it in there. Maybe I am overlooking it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e a (non-bane) weapon deals bashing damage to ephemeral entities <i>if</i> it is in the same frequency of twilight, is in the appropriate realm (Shadow, the Underworld), or the entity has the Materialized tag; otherwise physical objects do not interact with ephemeral beings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see in the new ruleset they have made some sort of sanity system called Integrity, so that's great. I was looking for that as well. </div> </div> </div>Integrity replaced Morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So I only need to make a conversion of the Second Sight magic system or just use the old rules instead. But I do like the complete package the new ruleset offers. I think the core rules provide for the same stuff you needed at least four books in the previous edition. </div> </div> </div>There is a fan supplement called <i>Second Sight: Third Eye</i> that's really good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}